A||||4||Formula88||AAARRRRRGGGHHHHH!!!!!   @#$@%||||8||
Z||000000||Formula88||11-11-2001||02:45 PM||||AAAHHH!  Ok, I'm putting my new KYB shocks and struts on my Formula this weekend.  No sweat, right?  WRONG!  Had to cut the bolts off of both front shocks (can you say original shocks?) - busted 1 nut splitter, got another, broke the shock shaft off in my shock absorber socket, got another one, finally got the shocks on.  That was the easy part.  Now for the rear struts.....<P>No big deal, other than needing a 4' long breaker bar to get the lower strut bolts loose - then, D!@%$@#$%@ - rounded off the top shaft on the strut trying to take the spring off..... ok, no panic - back to Sears for some more Craftsman.  Get a 10mm, 6 point, 1/2" drive socket, lots of Liquid Wrench and let it soak over night last night.  Today, finally get the bolt off - get the springs on the new struts, driver's side strut in --- COOL, one side to go, I'm almost done!  WRONG!  I've got the passenger side strut in, but I CANNOT get one of the bottom strut bolts in to save my a$$!  I'm only off by about 1mm or so - SOOO CLOSE, but no matter how much I yank, pull, twist, or cuss, it's just not going through!!!<P>Ok.  Taking a break now.  Had to vent.  Feeling a bit better now.  Gonna head back out to try and tackle it some more in a bit.  Just thought I'd share my frustration.  Thanks for listening.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>FYI: I'm using KYB Gas-A-Just front, and KYB GR-2 struts in the rear.  The struts are listed by Tire Rack.com as 84-87 (they show no listing for 88), but they are identical to the OEM struts I pulled off.  The bolt that's giving me a PITA was also a PITA to get out of the OEM strut, too.||||reg||8
Z||000001||pherder||11-11-2001||03:19 PM||||The reason you are having so much problems is because the KYB struts are not made to fit the 88s WITHOUT a small mod to the strut that you are going to use on the passenger's side.<P>Here is the interference:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/KYBmods1.jpg"> <P>Here is the place I ground on mine:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/KYBmods2.jpg"> <P>Paul||||reg||3
Z||000002||Formula88||11-11-2001||06:02 PM||||Well, that would explain it.  That's exactly the problem I was having - but I managed to get in on without grinding anything down.  Took some serious grunting, but it worked.  Car seems to run fine, other than needing a 4-wheel alignment (scheduled for tomorrow).<P><BR><B><FONT SIZE="3"><I><FONT COLOR="RED">BUT WAIT -- IT GET'S BETTER!!!</B></FONT></I></FONT><P>I take the car out for a test drive.  Everthing seems to be running fine...no problems.  So I head over to Advance Auto to return my Sturt Spring Compressor.  As I'm pulling into Advance Auto I notice a strange sound coming from the engine compartment.  Did I leave something loose?  Is something not right with the struts?  Hmmm.  So, I return the spring compressor, come back and get in the car, turn the key and she fires right up.  And then stalls immediately.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  Ok, try again - same thing.  Start again, this time keep it running by revving it a bit - LOUD SCREECHING NOISE accompanied by white smoke and my <FONT COLOR="red">VOLTS</FONT> light is on.  It appears my alternator decided to seize up. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  Only thing I can figure is I ran the battery low listening to the radio while working on the car and it burnt out the alternator when it tried to charge it back up.  Thing is, the car started fine and all the gauges looked good on the way to Advance.  Oh, well.  I just got back home (taxi cab).  Advance can't get a replacement alternator 'till Tues. and it's $89.  I'm gonna try to find one in stock somewhere tomorrow and go from there.<P>I love my car.  I really do!  But damn, what luck.  At least it died at the auto parts store.  Just hope they don't mind me changing an alternator in the parking lot, cuz that's what I'm gonna do.<P>Later.||||reg||8
Z||000003||mrfiero||11-11-2001||06:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pherder:<BR><B>The reason you are having so much problems is because the KYB struts are not made to fit the 88s WITHOUT a small mod to the strut that you are going to use on the passenger's side.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Just another FYI......not all '88s need this modification.  I just installed KYB struts and lowered springs on my '88 GT a few weeks ago and had no problems.  <P>It's been my experience that about half need the mod and half don't.  I've installed KYB struts on 5 '88 Fieros and only 2 needed some help to fit right.   <P>Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||11-11-2001||06:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pherder:<BR><B>The reason you are having so much problems is because the KYB struts are not made to fit the 88s WITHOUT a small mod to the strut that you are going to use on the passenger's side.<BR>Paul</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Paul, THANKS!  Info like that is why I love this forum!!  ||||reg||14
